{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.LocallyUniformLimit","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdFactorAnalytic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire.phiBProd_den_analytic_of_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire.phiBProd_den_analytic_of_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LocalUniformLimitEntire.lean#L59-L66","doc":"**The denominator infinite product is entire, given local-uniform convergence.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire.phiBProd_num_analytic_of_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire.phiBProd_num_analytic_of_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LocalUniformLimitEntire.lean#L48-L57","doc":"**The numerator infinite product is entire, given local-uniform convergence.** The\npartial products `∏_{k ∈ range n} numFactor b · k` are entire (`analyticOnNhd_numPartial`);\nif they converge locally uniformly to the `tprod`, that product is entire. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire.analyticOnNhd_of_tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire.analyticOnNhd_of_tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LocalUniformLimitEntire.lean#L36-L46","doc":"**Local-uniform limit of analytic functions is analytic** (Weierstrass + Cauchy).\nA sequence `F n` analytic on an open `s ⊆ ℂ`, converging locally uniformly to `g`, has an\nanalytic limit `g`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}